# Runtime validation artifacts — overwritten on each run, not source truth.
output/latest_validation_summary.json
output/latest_validation_summary.txt
output/notion_stage*.md

# Phase-0 regression contract fixtures — committed on purpose (overrides the
# repo-root "*.mat" ignore). These frozen golden references ARE the contract.
!tests/regression/golden/*.mat
!tests/regression/baselines/configuration/configuration_snapshots.mat
!tests/regression/baselines/configuration/configuration_resolution_manifest.json
# ...but the hand-made snapshot taken BESIDE a golden before re-cutting it is not a
# contract, it is an undo buffer. README_regression_golden.md documents the convention, so
# these keep appearing: one file per golden per re-cut, ~50 kB each. Neither ignore rule
# above caught them — the repo-root "*.mat" requires the name to END in .mat, and
# "golden_full.mat.pre_r_fixes" does not — so 25 of them (1.2 MB of binary blobs) surfaced
# as untracked and were one click away from being committed into history permanently.
# Delete them once the re-cut is trusted; never version them.
*.mat.pre_*
# Phase-7 report .tex byte-diff reference (overrides the repo-root "*.txt" ignore).
!tests/report/golden_report_tex.txt
# User-facing scenario overlays — committed on purpose (overrides the repo-root "*.json" ignore).
# The 2026-08-08 migration replaced config/scenarios/ with config/ + config/ladder/<axis>/,
# which silently un-negated this rule: every NEW ladder JSON became invisible to `git add`,
# while the pre-migration files stayed tracked because git keeps tracking what is already in
# the index. Five band files and two whole axes went unversioned before it was noticed. The
# axis wildcard is deliberate so a new ladder axis is versioned the moment it is created.
!config/*.json
!config/ladder/*/*.json
tests/regression/full_gate_marker.txt
tests/regression/verify_report_marker.txt

# Ladder sweep OUTPUT directories. These are run artefacts (reports, .mat, figures)
# regenerated by run_irp_ladder_sweep, not sources -- large binaries that would bloat
# history and conflict between concurrent sweeps. The "HEAD" variant is the snapshot
# copy a sweep leaves behind. Deliberately NOT covered by the config/*.json negations
# above, which exist to keep ladder SCENARIO files versioned.
IRP Ladder Results/
IRP Ladder Results HEAD/
# The two rules above did not cover the sweeps that actually exist on disk. "IRP Ladder
# Results Final" is 2.4 GB and "IRP Multipath State AB" is 58 MB, both untracked and both
# one `git add -A` away from being written into history permanently, where they could not
# be removed without rewriting it. The wildcard is deliberate: the next sweep will invent
# another suffix and must be caught before someone stages it, not after.
IRP Ladder Results*/
IRP Multipath State*/
# Ladder REPORT directories under output/ -- the aggregated PDF/PNG/mat artefacts a sweep
# leaves behind, 13.4 MB across four of them today. output/Report-*, Sweep_* and friends
# were already ignored above; this family was not.
output/LadderReport_*/
# Final-run configuration overlays. Held out of version control on request while the
# numbers they produce are still moving. NOTE these are scenario SOURCES, not artefacts,
# so this rule is the odd one out here: if the final configuration is ever quoted in a
# result, it has to come back under version control or the result is untraceable.
config/final/
